   "headline": "Seoul shares rebound more than 6% as chipmakers recover",
   "when": "Tue 24 Nov · Seoul close",
   "what": "The KOSPI rose 297.49 points, or 6.32%, to 5,006.03, ending a two-day slide. Samsung Electronics gained 6.7% and SK hynix 6.73%. Foreign investors bought a net 725.6 billion won, institutions 869 billion won, and individuals sold 2 trillion won. The won strengthened to 1,342.4 per dollar. SK hynix's sales to Nvidia were close to 15% of its revenue in the first nine months of 2026.",
